                <pb facs="0731" n="613" sameAs="frus:frus1928v02/pg613"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">821.6363 Barco/88: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Colombia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Piles</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bogotá</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-04-02T17:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 2, 1928—5
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received April 3—7:33
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>25. My 24, April 1, 11 a.m. I regard it extremely important that the company
                    immediately send Mr. Jordan Herbert Stabler to Bogotá with full power to act, as
                    I have been given to understand that his presence here would greatly facilitate
                    a settlement. He is close friend of the Foreign Minister, who desires to talk
                    with him. I feel confident that the matter can be satisfactorily settled within
                    a month or so.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Piles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
